a congressional panel led by democrats  has been investigating the january 6th  riot  now after conducting nearly a thousand  interviews and collecting 250 terabytes  of data the panel will finally begin to  reveal its findings to the public trump  was prepared to seize the presidency and  likely to invoke the insurrection act  and declare martial law so we're going  to tell the whole story of everything  that happened  thursday will be the first of several  public hearings they'll feature live  witnesses and previously unseen videos  from january 6. i think  people would want to see some new  information  and particularly new striking  information about trump's involvement  videotaped depositions of trump's  daughter and son-in-law may be shown at  the hearings but trump himself is not  expected to testify we fight like hell  and if you don't fight like hell you're  not going to have a country anymore  last year he was impeached for inciting  insurrection but was not convicted among  the answers that may be revealed what  trump was doing as his supporters  stormed the capitol and why he waited  three hours to call them off you have to  go home now  we have to have peace trump has not  faced criminal charges whether that  changes after these public hearings is  uncertain  the hearings will also delve further  into security failures in the days ahead  of january 6 and efforts by trump and  his aides to overturn the election  january 6 was a very dark day in  america's history i think it's important  to have a full accounting of what  happened  and making sure that through these  hearings  we ensure that it doesn't happen again  republicans call the democrat-led  investigation a sham a recent nbc news  poll shows the percentage of americans  who believe trump was responsible for  the riot has dropped to 45 percent and  it's unclear how many people will tune  into this round of hearings but  democrats are hoping for another chance  at a public reckoning  that may help the party in november's  midterm elections  heidi jo castro al jazeera washington
 

